{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1254562-gargoyle-classic","id":1254562,"title":"Gargoyle Classic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-15T10:57:53-07:00","id":1254562,"title":"Gargoyle Classic","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> In the COTD scenario, which creature could be classified a classic gargoyle (that one in statue form, that transforms in a giant bat outside the castle)? Should be a Spirit? Demon? A kind of vampire? What do you suggest.<br /> <br /> FYI: the actual campaign is a medieval scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T11:11:01-07:00","id":1254564,"title":"","content":"CofD and Hunter: the Vigil presume there are many unknown forces in the darkness, many of which are unique monsters not explained or accounted for by any particular monster gameline. The simplest answer, therefore, is that the gargoyle is a gargoyle. It doesn't need to be anything else specifically, and a cabal of hunters might not even necessarily ever find out what circumstances spawned it (though they certainly might in some stories). Both the CofD and Hunter cores provide some rules for building powers for unique monsters.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for precedents in other gamelines because you want to dig for further idea fodder:<ul><li>Vampire: the Requiem presents various blood rituals by which the Kindred animate stone with the power of the blood as loyal gargoyle servitors, often but not always to guard their havens during the daytime. These are the most obvious choices for prewritten gargoyles in the classic style.</li> <li>Promethean: the Created's Pandorans are botched, bestial chimeras which turn to stone and are mistaken for statuary except when roused by opportunities to predate and feed on the life-energies they devour. A more intelligent gargoyle might be a shapeshifting Promethean golem in seclusion whose flesh of clay is veiled by an illusion until he unleashes his power. The two ideas could also be combined, with one golem Centimanus intentionally cobbling Pandorans together as monstrous slaves.</li> <li>The conspiratorial works of Demon: the Descent's God-Machine sometimes produce occult mutations in surrounding wildlife. Ordinary bats or raptors swelling to fearsome sizes and developing petrified shells could certainly cause problems and start ill rumors about the land that produces them.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T12:22:43-07:00","id":1254582,"title":"","content":"I would also suggest the creation of a mage using life and matter magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T12:37:41-07:00","id":1254593,"title":"","content":"It might be better to ask what source <i>can't</i> produce gargoyles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T12:03:27-07:00","id":1256189,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve made mummy Relics which come from Effigies. And I would think you could make a whole game line based off Disney\u2019s Gargoyles, we did it all the time in the Classic World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}